  "narrative": "All outcome_006 comparisons are direction -1, so positive signed estimates mean stronger dependency in feature_060=1 than feature_060=0. The outcome_006 absolute mean is about 0.175, so the 10% clinical threshold is approximately 0.0175 score units.\n\nH145 (feature_024>=Q3 simple effect) and H146 (high-quartile direct interaction) are the most interesting new results. H145 is +0.0631, about 36.0% of the absolute outcome scale, with adequate cells 249/251, but its 95% interval crosses zero (-0.0074 to +0.1335). H146 is +0.0583, about 33.2%, with adequate cells, but is also imprecise (-0.0226 to +0.1392). Because these are discovery-only refinements of a family of feature_024 threshold tests, and both intervals include zero, I keep them unresolved and active rather than accept them. I request validation of H146 because direct interaction is the central unresolved question: whether feature_024 genuinely modifies the feature_060 association rather than merely selecting a subgroup with a different baseline feature_060 contrast.\n\nThe lower and middle feature_024 bands support, but do not prove, concentration in the high tail. H147 is a low-quartile negative control with estimate +0.0087, below threshold, and is rejected/closed. H148 (median-to-Q3 band) is +0.0164, slightly below threshold and imprecise; I leave it unresolved but closed because it is less informative than H145/H146 and does not warrant follow-up. H150/H151 test the extreme tail feature_024>=-4.0 and have large point estimates (+0.0748 and +0.0594), but cells are small (66/64) and intervals are extremely wide. I close them as unresolved due to fragility and multiple threshold exploration.\n\nThe feature_034 decomposition is important. H152 estimates the feature_060 contrast within feature_024>=median and feature_034=1: +0.0673, about 38.3%, with adequate cells and a 95% interval excluding zero (+0.0012 to +0.1334). This is striking but remains a nested selected subgroup, so I do not accept it yet; I keep it active for possible validation. H153, the feature_034=0 complement within high feature_024, is near null (+0.0111, about 6.3%) and rejected. The pattern suggests the high-feature_024 signal may be concentrated with feature_034=1, but the existing H154 interaction was incorrectly specified with identical eligibility and subgroup conditions and therefore has no valid complement; I closed it and registered a corrected interaction (eligibility feature_024>=median, subgroup feature_034=1) to directly test this overlap later.\n\nOutcome-specificity checks are null or unfavorable in the same high-feature_024 subgroup: H155 outcome_008 simple effect is +0.0025; H158 outcome_008 interaction is -0.0079; H156 outcome_011 is -0.0084 (opposite direction); and H157 outcome_013 is +0.0196, below its approximately 0.0269 threshold. These support the interpretation that the current signal is specific to outcome_006, but do not establish causality or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset-specific association: H142, outcome_006 feature_060=1 vs 0 among feature_024 >= median, with independent validation. Central active question is whether feature_024 genuinely modifies feature_060 association.\n\nNew high-quartile evidence: H145 simple effect +0.0631 (interval crosses zero), H146 high-quartile direct interaction +0.0583 (interval crosses zero). These are the strongest unvalidated candidates; request validation of H146. Keep H145 and H146 active. If H146 validates positively, consider accepting a high-quartile effect-modification claim and then follow feature_034 interaction. If H146 validates null, retain H142 but downgrade feature_024 modification claims.\n\nGradient controls: H147 low quartile near null/reject. H148 median-Q3 band below threshold; closed unresolved. H150/H151 extreme tail promising but small/underpowered and multiple-selected; closed unresolved.\n\nFeature_034 decomposition: H152 high feature_024 + feature_034=1 simple effect +0.0673 with interval excluding zero, but nested selected subgroup; keep active. H153 high feature_024 + feature_034=0 near null/reject. H154 original interaction was invalid (identical eligibility/subgroup, empty complement) and closed. New proposal: outcome_006 feature_060 interaction eligibility feature_024>=median, subgroup feature_034=1, parent H152, to directly test overlap.\n\nOutcome specificity: H155 outcome_008 null, H156 outcome_011 opposite/near null, H157 outcome_013 below threshold, H158 outcome_008 interaction opposite/null; all reject/close. This strengthens outcome_006 specificity but not causal or generalizable claims. H149 redundant lower-middle band closed. Keep H144 active as the median-split interaction; H146 is the high-quartile refinement.",
